  "notes": "Camden County Republicans elect county committee by municipality, not by election district: the official 2026 primary report has a 'REP Male Members of County Committee' and a 'REP Female Members of County Committee' contest for each of 36 municipalities (Camden City, Gloucester City and Winslow labeled At-Large), each Vote For N with N from 1 (e.g. Audubon Park) to 24 (Cherry Hill). Each entry in precincts is a municipality with N Committeeman and N Committeewoman seats (316 seats in all), so seats_per_precinct is null. No Democratic county committee contests were on the 2026 ballot; the Republican committee contests on the June 2, 2026 ballot are the most recent Republican election found. Filled = a named ballot candidate placed within the top N among ballot candidates with more votes than that contest's total write-in votes (so no write-in could have outpolled them), and no tie at the cutoff. Slots printed as 'NO PETITION FILED' had no ballot candidate; for each contest the open seats (N minus ballot winners) are counted unknown up to the number of write-in votes cast (each write-in winner needs at least one vote) and empty beyond that, so a contest with zero write-in votes has all open seats empty. Write-in winners are never treated as filled. The summary report is countywide by municipality, so NJ district-level privacy suppression does not affect these counts. No names are stored."
